.Pp
Build the artifacts declared in the
.Ql "info\&.edn"
in the current directory,
or in its
.Ql "pkg"
subdirectory.
.Ic build exe
makes a single-file executable for each
.Ql ":exe" ,
containing the Wattle runtime,
the compiled program and the native modules it links.
.Ic build lib
makes a shared library for each
.Ql ":lib" .
.Ic build web
makes,
for each
.Ql ":web" ,
an image of the program,
a Wattle runtime built for WebAssembly that loads an image,
and the JavaScript that runs them in a browser.
If
.Ar name
is given,
only the artifact of that name is built.
The results are in
.Ql "zig-out"
in the current directory.
The project needs no
.Ql "build\&.zig" .
.Pp
Both commands need Zig on the
.Ql "PATH"
and the Wattle package,
which
.Ic zig build
installs in
.Ql "share/wattle" ,
under
.Ql "*prefix*" .
They write a
.Ql "build\&.zig"
and a
.Ql "build\&.zig\&.zon"
in
.Ql "\&.zig-cache/wattle-build"
and run
.Ic zig build
on them.
Each error in
.Ql "info\&.edn" ,
and a missing Zig,
is reported on one line and the exit status is 1.
.Pp
The
.Ql "info\&.edn"
declares the artifacts in a vector,
in the
.Ql ":artifacts"
key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqgreeter\(dq
 :artifacts \(lB{:type :lib
              :name \(dqgreet\(dq
              :root \(dqgreet\&.zig\(dq}
             {:type :exe
              :name \(dqhello\(dq
              :entry \(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq
              :libs \(lB\(dqgreet\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.Pp
Every artifact has a
.Ql ":type" ,
.Ql ":exe" ,
.Ql ":lib"
or
.Ql ":web" ,
and a
.Ql ":name"
of letters,
digits,
.Ql "_"
and
.Ql "-"
that is unique in the project.
An
.Ql ":exe"
has an
.Ql ":entry" ,
the Wattle file that defines
.Ql "main" ,
and may have
.Ql ":libs" ,
the names of the
.Ql ":lib"
artifacts linked into it.
A
.Ql ":lib"
has a
.Ql ":root" ,
the Zig root file of a native module.
A
.Ql ":web"
has an
.Ql ":entry"
and no other key.
Relative paths are relative to the current directory.
.Pp
.Ic build web
writes
.Ql "zig-out/web/<name>/"
with four files:
.Ql "wattle-<hash>\&.wasm" ,
the runtime;
.Ql "<name>-<hash>\&.wimage" ,
the program;
.Ql "wasi-<hash>\&.js" ,
the WASI support;
and
.Ql "<name>\&.js" ,
an ES module that exports
.Ql "run"
and imports the support.
.Ql "<hash>"
is the same in the three names.
It is sixteen hexadecimal digits of a SHA-256 over the contents
of the runtime,
the image and the support,
so a change to any of them gives all three new names and files
with the same hash belong together.
.Ql "<name>\&.js"
keeps its name and refers to the other three.
.Ql "load"
fetches the runtime and the image once,
compiles the runtime and returns an object with
.Ql "run" .
.Ql "run"
takes
.Ql "args" ,
an array of strings,
and
.Ql "stdin" ,
a string or a
.Ql "Uint8Array" .
It loads the image,
calls its
.Ql "main"
with the arguments as they are,
so the first is the program’s name by the convention of
.Ic wattle -i ,
and returns an object with
.Ql "status" ,
.Ql "stdout" ,
.Ql "stderr"
and
.Ql "error" .
Standard input reads
.Ql "stdin"
to its end.
The first
.Ql "run"
starts an instance of the runtime and later calls use it.
A call that traps or exits leaves no usable instance and the
next call starts another,
and
.Ql "fresh: true"
starts one for that call.
.Ql "run"
exported from the module is
.Ql "load"
and one call.
Both take the URLs of the two files as
.Ql "wasm"
and
.Ql "image"
when they are not beside the module.
The runtime has no parser and no compiler,
so the program cannot call
.Ql "eval" ,
.Ql "parse"
or
.Ql "run-context" ,
and it has no docstrings or source maps.
The runtime is built for
.Ql "wasm32-wasi"
and
.Ic build web
takes no
.Fl t .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
